IMPORT prelude

-- Street Works Act 1995 (Singapore) -- what a landowner, builder, contractor or shopkeeper meets: stopping damaging activity next
-- to a public street (s 8), engineering works near a road structure (s 8A), the Authority's entry on private land and the owner's
-- right to require acquisition (ss 9, 10A(5), 11, 13(3)), works on public streets (s 17), obstructing streets and footways (s 32A),
-- damaging public streets (s 33), mandatory orders and appeals (ss 35, 36), removing marks (s 39), recovery of sums (s 40(2)),
-- general penalties (s 49), composition (s 52) and the cap on regulation fines (s 53(4)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/SWA1995.txt, with amendments to
-- Act 42 of 2022 (in force 1 November 2024) shown.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 11 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to duties, offences, notice periods and
-- penalties an ordinary person or business meets. Not encoded: the Authority's construction powers (ss 5-7), creation of rights
-- (s 10), the acquisition procedure (s 11A), street reserves and cost apportionment (ss 14-16), private streets and deposits
-- (ss 18-26), footways, utilities and backlanes (ss 27-31), recovery machinery (ss 41-45), service, evidence and the Schedule of
-- regulation subjects. No regulations under s 53 were read.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Street Works Act 1995 -- works and offences`

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` MEANS
    IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

DECLARE Place IS ONE OF
    `a public street`
    `a public bridge`
    `a street to be declared public`
    `a private street`
    `a five-footway`
    `a private footway`

§§ `8 -- activity damaging a public street`

-- s 8(1): where an activity "on any land adjoining a public street has caused or is likely to cause the public street ... to be in a
-- dangerous or defective condition", the Authority may by notice require repair, repair and recover costs, require the activity to
-- stop until a deposit is made, or order immediate stoppage. (5): "activity" includes any excavation or construction works.
-- s 8(3): contravening a notice or order -- fine up to $10,000 or imprisonment up to 12 months or both; a further fine up to $500 for
-- every day the notice was not complied with; and a further $500 for every day the contravention continues after conviction.
GIVEN `activity on adjoining land` IS A BOOLEAN, `caused or likely to cause a dangerous or defective public street` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Authority may act under s 8` IF
    `activity on adjoining land` AND `caused or likely to cause a dangerous or defective public street`

GIVEN `days the notice was not complied with` IS A NUMBER, `days continuing after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 8 maximum fine` MEANS
    10000 PLUS 500 TIMES `days the notice was not complied with` PLUS 500 TIMES `days continuing after conviction`

`the s 8 maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS 12

§§ `8A -- engineering works in the road structure safety zone`

-- s 8A(1): "A person must not carry out any engineering works within the road structure safety zone unless the person has obtained
-- the prior approval of the Authority." (4): "engineering works" is construction work "likely to affect the structural integrity of
-- any road structure", including basement excavation, piling, bore holes, ground anchors and operating a crane or heavy equipment;
-- the zone is the land "which is 20 metres from the outermost edge of any part of a road structure".
-- (Inference: "within ... 20 metres" is read as at most 20 metres, inclusive.)
-- s 8A(3): fine up to $5,000 and $100 for every day or part of a day the offence continues after conviction. No imprisonment.
GIVEN `metres from the road structure` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `within the road structure safety zone` IF
    `metres from the road structure` AT MOST 20

GIVEN `engineering works` IS A BOOLEAN, `metres from the road structure` IS A NUMBER, `prior approval of the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under s 8A` IF
        `engineering works`
    AND `within the road structure safety zone` `metres from the road structure`
    AND (NOT `prior approval of the Authority`)

GIVEN `days continuing after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 8A maximum fine` MEANS
    5000 PLUS 100 TIMES `days continuing after conviction`

§§ `9, 10A, 11, 13 -- entry on private land, notice periods, acquisition`

-- s 9(2): the Authority "must not exercise the right" to enter and take possession of private land "unless the Authority has given at
-- least 2 months' notice ... to every owner and occupier of the land". s 9(5): refusing access to, or obstructing, hindering or
-- delaying, an agent or employee -- fine up to $1,000.
GIVEN `months of notice given` IS A NUMBER, `notice given to every owner and occupier` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Authority may enter private land under s 9` IF
    `months of notice given` AT LEAST 2 AND `notice given to every owner and occupier`

`the s 9 obstruction maximum fine` MEANS 1000

-- s 13(3)(c): a notice to remove an object or structure from land in the street reserve must "be given to the owner ... not later than
-- 28 days before the commencement of" the removal period.
GIVEN `days before the removal period begins` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 13 removal notice is in time` IF
    `days before the removal period begins` AT LEAST 28

-- s 10A(5): where no meter is installed on non-State land, the Authority must pay the electricity supplier monthly
-- "P x R x 24 hours x 30 days", P being the power rating of the equipment and R the supplier's rate.
GIVEN `power rating` IS A NUMBER, `rate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 10A monthly electricity payment` MEANS
    `power rating` TIMES `rate` TIMES 24 TIMES 30

-- s 11(1): the owner of land temporary possession of which "is or has been taken in accordance with section 9" may by written notice
-- request the Government to acquire it (and related land) if the owner considers it suffers "substantial impairment" of its rights.
-- (2): if there is more than one owner, the notice "must be given by all the owners". (3): the notice is irrevocable.
-- (5): "owner" means (a) the fee simple holder; (b) a grantee or lessee under a State title; (c) a person entitled to exercise a power
-- of sale; or (d) "a person in occupation of the land under a tenancy the term of which exceeds 7 years".
DECLARE Interest IS ONE OF
    `fee simple`
    `State title grantee or lessee`
    `mortgagee entitled to exercise a power of sale`
    `occupying tenant`
    `licensee`

GIVEN `the interest` IS A Interest, `tenancy term in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an owner for s 11` IF
    CONSIDER `the interest`
    WHEN `fee simple` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `State title grantee or lessee` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `mortgagee entitled to exercise a power of sale` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `occupying tenant` THEN `tenancy term in years` GREATER THAN 7
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the interest` IS A Interest, `tenancy term in years` IS A NUMBER, `temporary possession taken under s 9` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `considers rights substantially impaired` IS A BOOLEAN, `notice joined by all the owners` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may require acquisition under s 11` IF
        `an owner for s 11` `the interest` `tenancy term in years`
    AND `temporary possession taken under s 9`
    AND `considers rights substantially impaired`
    AND `notice joined by all the owners`

§§ `17 -- works on public streets`

-- s 17(1): "A person must not carry out any works on any public street, public bridge or on any street which is to be declared public
-- unless the person has obtained the prior approval of the Authority." (4): the Authority may order cessation, removal,
-- reinstatement or alteration of works carried out in contravention. (8): failing to comply with such an order -- fine up to
-- $100,000 and $1,000 for every day the offence continues after conviction.
-- s 17(1) itself is not declared an offence in the text read; the criminal sanction is attached to the s 17(4) order.
-- A five-footway or private footway is not named in s 17(1) and is not decided here.
GIVEN `the place` IS A Place
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `works need the Authority's prior approval under s 17` IF
    CONSIDER `the place`
    WHEN `a public street` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a public bridge` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a street to be declared public` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `days continuing after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 17 order maximum fine` MEANS
    100000 PLUS 1000 TIMES `days continuing after conviction`

§§ `32A -- obstructing public streets, five-footways and private footways`

-- s 32A(1): a person must not deposit an article, cause or allow it to remain on or protrude over, or erect a structure on, under or
-- over "any public street, five-footway or private footway ... so as to create any obstruction or inconvenience to the passage of the
-- public". (2): contravention is an offence. (16): the section "does not apply in relation to any public path (within the meaning of
-- the Active Mobility Act 2017) that is not on State land".
-- (4): before moving or removing anything, an authorised officer must take reasonable steps to inform the owner, the person
-- responsible, or the frontager (if known), "and allowed or directed the person to move or remove" it. (6), (7): failing without
-- reasonable excuse to move it when directed is an offence. (14): for (2) or (7), fine up to $2,000 and $100 for every day or part
-- of a day the offence continues after conviction.
GIVEN `the place` IS A Place
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 32A covers the place` IF
    CONSIDER `the place`
    WHEN `a public street` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a five-footway` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a private footway` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the place` IS A Place, `deposited, left or erected something` IS A BOOLEAN, `obstructs or inconveniences the public` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a public path not on State land` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an obstruction offence under s 32A` IF
        `s 32A covers the place` `the place`
    AND `deposited, left or erected something`
    AND `obstructs or inconveniences the public`
    AND (NOT `a public path not on State land`)

GIVEN `took reasonable steps to inform and allowed removal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an officer may remove the obstruction` IF
    `took reasonable steps to inform and allowed removal`

GIVEN `directed to remove it` IS A BOOLEAN, `removed it` IS A BOOLEAN, `reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence of failing to remove under s 32A(7)` IF
    `directed to remove it` AND (NOT `removed it`) AND (NOT `reasonable excuse`)

GIVEN `days continuing after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 32A maximum fine` MEANS
    2000 PLUS 100 TIMES `days continuing after conviction`

-- s 32A(11): sale proceeds go "(a) ... in payment of any expenses incurred in removing, storing and disposing" and "(b) thereafter ...
-- in payment of all charges and fines payable", and "the surplus (if any) must be paid to the owner ... or if not claimed by such
-- owner within 12 months of the date of the sale, is forfeited to the Authority".
GIVEN `proceeds` IS A NUMBER, `removal and storage expenses` IS A NUMBER, `charges and fines` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the surplus on sale` MEANS
    IF `proceeds` MINUS `removal and storage expenses` MINUS `charges and fines` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN `proceeds` MINUS `removal and storage expenses` MINUS `charges and fines`
    ELSE 0

GIVEN `months after sale when claimed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the surplus is forfeited` IF
    `months after sale when claimed` GREATER THAN 12

§§ `33 -- damaging public streets`

-- s 33(1): an offence if the person "intentionally, recklessly or negligently engages in conduct that causes damage" to a public street
-- (or Government property in, on or under it), (b) without "the prior written approval of the Authority", and (c) the damage
-- "prevents or substantially prevents the passage of pedestrians or vehicular traffic on or other use of the public street".
-- (2): intentionally -- fine up to $100,000 or imprisonment up to 6 months or both; any other case -- fine up to $50,000 or 6 months.
-- (3): "Whether or not any proceedings ... are instituted or result in a conviction", the Authority may recover "the full amount of
-- the damage caused" from "any person who engaged in conduct that caused damage". No fault element is stated in (3).
DECLARE Fault IS ONE OF
    `intentionally`
    `recklessly`
    `negligently`
    `without fault`

GIVEN `the fault` IS A Fault
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a fault element of s 33` IF
    CONSIDER `the fault`
    WHEN `without fault` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the fault` IS A Fault, `prior written approval` IS A BOOLEAN, `prevents or substantially prevents use` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under s 33` IF
        `a fault element of s 33` `the fault`
    AND (NOT `prior written approval`)
    AND `prevents or substantially prevents use`

GIVEN `the fault` IS A Fault
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 33 maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the fault`
    WHEN `intentionally` THEN 100000
    OTHERWISE 50000

`the s 33 maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS 6

GIVEN `the damage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount the Authority may recover under s 33(3)` MEANS `the damage`

§§ `35, 36 -- mandatory orders and appeals`

-- s 35(2)(a): a person who fails to comply with a mandatory order is guilty of an offence, "unless the person satisfies the court that
-- the person has used all due diligence", and liable to "a fine not exceeding $500 a day during the person's default".
-- s 36(1): an appeal lies to the Minister "within 14 days from the date of the order", and "no liability to a fine under
-- section 35(2)(a) shall arise ... until after the determination or abandonment of the appeal". (The words "until after" are read here
-- as governing the fine as well as proceedings and work -- an inference from the sentence structure.)
GIVEN `appealed` IS A BOOLEAN, `days after the order the appeal was lodged` IS A NUMBER, `appeal determined or abandoned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an appeal under s 36 is pending` IF
    `appealed` AND `days after the order the appeal was lodged` AT MOST 14 AND (NOT `appeal determined or abandoned`)

GIVEN `failed to comply` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN, `days after the order the appeal was lodged` IS A NUMBER,
      `appealed` IS A BOOLEAN, `appeal determined or abandoned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `liable to a fine under s 35(2)(a)` IF
        `failed to comply`
    AND (NOT `proved due diligence`)
    AND (NOT `an appeal under s 36 is pending` `appealed` `days after the order the appeal was lodged` `appeal determined or abandoned`)

GIVEN `days in default` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 35 maximum fine` MEANS 500 TIMES `days in default`

§§ `39, 40, 49, 52, 53 -- marks, recovery, general penalty, composition, regulation fines`

-- s 39: removing "any mark set up for the purpose of indicating any level or direction" -- fine up to $2,000 or imprisonment up to
-- 3 months. s 49: an offence "for which no penalty is expressly provided" -- fine up to $2,000.
`the s 39 maximum fine` MEANS 2000
`the s 39 maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS 3
`the s 49 general maximum fine` MEANS 2000

-- s 40(2): an amount "not paid by the person liable ... within 14 days after demand" may be reported to the District Court and
-- recovered "as if it were a fine".
GIVEN `paid` IS A BOOLEAN, `days since demand` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may be recovered as if a fine under s 40(2)` IF
    (NOT `paid`) AND `days since demand` GREATER THAN 14

-- s 52(1)(a): for an offence "prescribed as being an offence which may be compounded", the Authority may collect "a sum not exceeding
-- the lower of" "(i) one half of the amount of the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence" and "(ii) $5,000".
GIVEN `the maximum fine` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 52 composition cap` MEANS
    `the lower of` (`the maximum fine` DIVIDED BY 2) 5000

-- s 53(4): a fine made by regulations "must not exceed for any one offence the sum of $2,000 and, in the case of a continuing offence,
-- the sum of $100 for every day or part of a day" after conviction.
GIVEN `fine` IS A NUMBER, `daily fine` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a regulation fine is within s 53(4)` IF
    `fine` AT MOST 2000 AND `daily fine` AT MOST 100
